From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 03:57:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 27/28] Guest verifier port between the tenants' ports and the
 ephemeral range; document the guest opt-in

The wasm manager starts before the verifier block in gsup, binds a tenant's declared port literally when it is free
(PORT_MAX_DECL 49999) and otherwise takes an OS port from the ephemeral range init pins at 58000-65535. A verifier port
in the tenants' range could be taken by a tenant while gsup restarts the verifier, which would then fail to bind until
that app stopped (verified reads refuse meanwhile). The checker now takes only 50000..57999, which no tenant can hold.
(The manager's bind audit polices tenant processes only, so the verifier's own listener is not policed.)

docs/network/local-chain-verifier.md gains the guest section: the config member, the checks and refusals, the start
order and names, what a consumer sees, copy staging and its RAM, rollback.
